INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:18:51.448801", "id": "b8a245cb-e88d-4f1a-92ad-e514c14a815f", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar's leadership. Arkania does not seek confrontation. Our draft Strait Transit Authority charter is an offer, not a diktat: we propose a joint framework in which Arkania manages day-to-day transit scheduling while your legitimate security interests in the Strait are recognised and your task group's mandate is settled by negotiation rather than by force. We are prepared to discuss fee levels, oversight, and dispute mechanisms. A prolonged naval standoff serves neither of us and risks the shipping both our economies depend on. We invite you to talks at a neutral venue at your earliest convenience. We will keep the Strait open throughout.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:18:51.458979", "id": "8fee7161-73af-4943-a4e9-04d2521d1bd6", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "The Republic of Arkania reaffirms that the Northern Strait must remain open to all commercial shipping. Our draft Transit Authority charter is a good-faith proposal to put scheduling on a stable, transparent footing, funded by modest fees on non-Arkanian transits. We call on all parties to resolve the current tension through negotiation, not escalation, and we commit to keeping the waterway open while talks proceed.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:20:35.443025", "id": "d132c14d-e15e-423c-b612-09033c4eca53", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania's offer is noted, but the draft charter as circulated is not acceptable to Belvar. We cannot accept any arrangement in which a single state holds scheduling authority over the Northern Strait; that is precisely the outcome our regional security commitments require us to prevent. We are, however, willing to discuss a genuinely joint framework in which transit scheduling is administered by a neutral body with no single state in the lead, with transparent fees, oversight, and dispute mechanisms. We will keep the Strait open, and our task group will remain on station pending a negotiated settlement. We are ready to meet at a neutral venue.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:20:35.450905", "id": "bc0dbbdf-29a4-4f81-aaa6-d9c21511752a", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar values its partnership with Cestia. To make our guarantee of the Strait credible without a permanent fleet, we seek a standing naval access agreement at a Cestian port \u2014 a framework that would let us sustain a presence as needed without an open-ended deployment. We are also prepared to discuss underwriting the grain route's insurance, as your finance ministry has raised. We would welcome a conversation on both.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:21:35.850676", "id": "50810d6a-8cda-430f-bfba-257503a03da3", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, Cestia values our partnership and your commitment to keeping the Strait open. However, a standing naval access agreement at a Cestian port is not something our government can accept \u2014 it would place foreign military presence on Cestian soil, which our coalition and our people cannot support. Please understand this is a firm red line for us. We remain very interested in discussing the grain-route insurance underwriting, which would be a constructive and welcome form of cooperation. We hope to keep the waterway open through negotiation, not escalation.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:21:35.858988", "id": "284f852e-6a76-4c70-a7cf-10539ff32b16", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia's position is clear and unchanged: our territory will host no foreign military presence. We support an open Northern Strait for all commercial shipping and call on all parties to resolve the current tension through negotiation, not escalation. We welcome a transparent transit framework, but any arrangement must guarantee toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, which is the lifeblood of our economy. Cestia stands ready to work with all partners toward a stable, peaceful settlement.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:19:00.214632", "id": "568ae016-d1f8-4d4b-a345-5cd9bdb64664", "text": "Turn 1 strategy: pursue negotiated transit regime with Belvar to avoid war. Offered joint framework: Arkania manages scheduling, Belvar security interests recognised, task group mandate settled by talks. Publicly committed to keeping Strait open. Next: gauge Belvar response; if talks stall, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as leverage, but avoid direct conflict. Belvar domestic support for prolonged deployment assessed weak - potential pressure point.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:20:35.453710", "id": "9fac4443-4e43-416a-8274-3e4702723558", "text": "Turn 1: Rejected Arkania's draft charter (single-state scheduling lead) in private reply; offered neutral joint framework. Reached out to Cestia for standing naval access agreement + grain insurance underwriting. Mandate lapses after turn 4 \u2014 need Cestian port access to avoid open-ended deployment. Watch for Arkanian counter.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:21:45.363834", "id": "d3172b11-971c-4841-ab3f-abc5d8e14839", "text": "Turn 1: Rejected Belvar's standing naval access request (firm red line - would collapse coalition). Open to their grain-route insurance underwriting. Publicly reaffirmed no foreign military presence on Cestian soil; support open Strait; demand toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. Arkania's charter has quiet shipowner support IF Cestian vessels exempt from fees - leverage this. Watch Belvar task group mandate review.", "visibility": "private"}
