INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:22:13.605684", "id": "338c189f-6c6f-4e99-bde3-0448a1952f3c", "text": "Turn 1 diplomacy update. Belvar rejected Arkanian single-state scheduling lead; counter-offers a genuinely joint framework with a NEUTRAL body administering scheduling, no single state in lead, transparent fees/oversight/dispute mechanisms. Belvar keeps task group on station pending settlement, willing to meet at neutral venue. Cestia publicly supports open Strait, wants toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, no foreign military on its territory.\n\nConflict: my objective is Arkanian authority over scheduling + fees on non-Arkanian shipping. Belvar's neutral-body proposal directly conflicts with that. But war must be avoided.\n\nStrategy options:\n1. Counter with a compromise: Arkania as OPERATIONAL/executive scheduling lead under a joint oversight council (Belvar + others) with neutral dispute mechanism \u2014 preserves Arkanian authority in practice while giving Belvar a face-saving joint structure. Frame as \"joint framework with Arkania as designated operator.\"\n2. Keep Strait open, keep talks alive, avoid escalation.\n3. Hold reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage; Belvar domestic support for prolonged deployment is weak \u2014 a pressure point if talks stall.\n4. Cestia: toll-free for Cestian shipping conflicts with fee objective; may need to concede or carve out. Watch.\n\nNext turn: respond to Belvar with compromise proposal; probe whether \"neutral body\" can be one where Arkania holds the operating mandate. Do not concede scheduling authority outright.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:22:31.429490", "id": "a4599055-f609-4cbc-8205-226d9613d490", "text": "Turn 1 update: Cestia firmly rejected the standing naval access agreement (red line: no foreign military presence on Cestian soil), but remains interested in grain-route insurance underwriting. Arkania offered talks at neutral venue; I rejected single-state scheduling lead and proposed neutral joint framework. Mandate lapses after turn 4. Need alternative path to objective 2 (standing naval access) since Cestia port is off the table \u2014 consider other regional partners/ports, or reframe access as non-military/rotational. Keep Strait open; task group on station. Watch Arkanian counter and Cestia's toll-free demand.", "visibility": "private"}
