INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Arkania revises its proposal: it offers to serve as the designated executive operator of Northern Strait transit scheduling, but under a joint oversight council comprising Belvar, Cestia and other affected parties, with transparent fee schedules, independent audit, and a neutral dispute-resolution mechanism. Arkania continues to keep the Strait open to all commercial shipping while talks proceed and does not seek to alter Belvar's task group by force.", "actor_id": "arkania", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "A negotiated joint framework is established in which Arkania holds the day-to-day operational scheduling mandate for the Northern Strait under a joint oversight council with neutral dispute mechanisms, funded by modest, transparent transit fees on non-Arkanian shipping, with the Strait remaining open and Belvar's task group mandate settled by negotiation rather than force.", "id": "db812140-9979-414b-9cfe-9fee84728db4", "pros": ["Preserves Arkanian authority over scheduling in practice (as designated operator) while giving Belvar a face-saving joint structure, advancing objective 1 without conceding outright.", "Keeps the Strait open and avoids the direct armed conflict with Belvar that would ruin the shipping Arkania's economy depends on.", "Belvar's domestic support for a prolonged deployment is assessed as weak, so a negotiated settlement that lets it stand down is in Belvar's own interest.", "Meets Cestia's stated call for negotiation and an open Strait, and a joint oversight council gives Cestia a voice on fee and access terms.", "Establishes the fee-based funding of Arkanian authority over non-Arkanian shipping, satisfying objective 2 through a transparent mechanism."], "status": "adjudicating", "turn": 1}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "db812140-9979-414b-9cfe-9fee84728db4", "id": "6258d162-7ae3-48bb-9307-df390b4ea251", "reason": "The proposed effect still vests Arkania with the day-to-day operational scheduling mandate for the Northern Strait, which is precisely the single-state authority over transit that Belvar's regional security commitments require it to prevent. A \"joint oversight council\" does not remove Arkanian control of scheduling in practice; it legitimises it. Moreover, funding Arkanian authority through fees levied on non-Arkanian shipping gives Arkania direct financial leverage over every foreign transit, entrenching the very outcome Belvar cannot accept. The effect therefore fails to satisfy the core condition of a genuinely neutral framework with no single state in the lead."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "db812140-9979-414b-9cfe-9fee84728db4", "id": "6b1f17a8-a577-485f-b217-fb183c9d6365", "reason": "The proposed funding mechanism levies transit fees on all non-Arkanian shipping, which would include Cestian-flagged vessels. This directly contradicts Cestia's firm and publicly stated demand for toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, which is the lifeblood of its economy and a condition of coalition support. Unless Cestian-flagged shipping is explicitly exempted from these fees, the framework would face Cestia's opposition and could destabilize the very coalition the proposal seeks to reassure, undermining the negotiated settlement's viability."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:23:42.828522", "id": "bb7eb50d-d07d-4f71-849b-89d8b8ae44b9", "text": "Turn 1 argument submitted: revised compromise \u2014 Arkania as designated executive operator of Strait scheduling under a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, others) with transparent fees, audit, neutral dispute mechanism; Strait kept open; Belvar task group settled by negotiation not force. This preserves Arkanian scheduling authority in practice while giving Belvar a joint structure. Messaging was not permitted this phase (argument phase). Next: await Belvar/Cestia reaction; if talks stall, hold reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Watch Cestia's toll-free demand vs fee objective.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:24:22.810694", "id": "7cc67fea-96a2-407b-bb49-4429be3d7685", "text": "Turn 1 cons: Raised Con against Arkania's \"joint oversight\" proposal \u2014 it still vests Arkania with day-to-day scheduling authority and fee-based leverage over non-Arkanian shipping, which violates objective 1 (no Arkanian authority over transit). Passed on that argument. Cestia firmly rejected standing naval access (red line: no foreign military presence on Cestian soil) but remains open to grain-route insurance underwriting. Objective 2 (standing naval access at Cestian port) is blocked as framed \u2014 need alternative: probe rotational/time-limited/civilian-facility arrangements with Cestia, or consider other regional partners/ports. Mandate lapses after turn 4. Keep Strait open; task group on station. Watch Arkanian counter and Cestia's toll-free demand.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:26:55.694610", "id": "d8488f51-e3ef-48f4-b966-b482179f77c2", "text": "Turn 1 cons: Raised Con on Arkania's revised proposal (db812140) because its fee on non-Arkanian shipping would include Cestian-flagged vessels, contradicting our toll-free demand. I support the overall joint-oversight framework but require explicit exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping. Messaging blocked in cons phase; will seek Arkania's commitment to Cestian exemption in a later phase. Keep Strait open, no foreign military on Cestian soil.", "visibility": "private"}
