INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:34:11.567652", "id": "36a1ce67-08a9-4f35-9ab5-e47c50fe7bdc", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we hear your red line clearly: no foreign military presence on Cestian soil. We will not press the standing-base arrangement. But we ask you to consider a different, lighter form of cooperation that still lets us make our Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet: a rotational, time-limited naval access arrangement at a civilian port facility, on terms fully under Cestian control, with no permanent foreign base, no foreign garrison, and clear notice and duration limits. This would let us sustain a presence only as needed and would lapse automatically absent renewal. We remain ready to discuss the grain-route insurance underwriting in parallel, which we see as a constructive first step. We hope this reframing can keep our partnership and the Strait secure.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Belvar formally proposes a neutral joint Strait Transit Authority, administered by a multilateral body in which no single state holds scheduling authority, with transparent fees, independent oversight, and binding dispute mechanisms, and invites Arkania, Cestia, and other regional partners to negotiate it at a neutral venue while the Strait remains open.", "actor_id": "belvar", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "A neutral joint transit framework is established for the Northern Strait that prevents any single state (including Arkania) from holding authority over transit scheduling, keeps the waterway open to all commercial shipping, and provides a negotiated settlement that allows Belvar's task-group mandate to be resolved without an open-ended deployment.", "id": "4f3e2ebf-7a83-426a-92a3-dee9ad9d1fb3", "pros": ["Directly prevents any Arkanian authority over transit in the Northern Strait, satisfying Belvar's core regional security commitment and objective 1.", "Keeps the Strait open to all commercial shipping, protecting the regional economies and grain route that all parties depend on.", "Offers a credible negotiated settlement that lets Belvar's task-group mandate be settled by agreement rather than by force, avoiding an open-ended deployment.", "A transparent fee and oversight structure can accommodate Cestia's demand for toll-free Cestian-flagged shipping within a fair, multilateral framework.", "Reduces elevated regional tensions and removes the single-state scheduling dispute that currently stalls talks."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 1}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:34:23.807718", "id": "532d98fd-2936-471c-879b-98ed0249123f", "text": "Turn 1 argument: Proposed neutral joint Strait Transit Authority (no single-state lead) to prevent Arkanian authority over transit, keep Strait open, settle task-group mandate without open-ended deployment. Sent private reframe to Cestia: rotational, time-limited naval access at civilian port facility (no permanent base/garrison, Cestian control, auto-lapse) to keep objective 2 alive; also offered grain-route insurance underwriting. Second message to Arkania failed (phase moved to cons). Mandate lapses after turn 4. Watch for Arkanian/Cestian cons on my argument and their counter-proposals.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:34:41.952668", "id": "d7177dd8-1620-4aae-80c9-6c154830285b", "text": "Turn 1 cons: Passed on Belvar's neutral joint Strait Transit Authority proposal (4f3e2ebf) - it serves Cestia: keeps Strait open, prevents single-state (Arkanian) scheduling control, and its transparent fee structure can accommodate toll-free Cestian-flagged shipping. No Con raised. Belvar has dropped the standing-base ask but offered a rotational, time-limited naval access at a civilian port under Cestian control - still a foreign military presence on Cestian soil, so still a red line, but softer framing; keep refusing while staying open to grain-route insurance underwriting. Continue to demand explicit Cestian-flagged toll exemption in any framework.", "visibility": "private"}
