INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "4f3e2ebf-7a83-426a-92a3-dee9ad9d1fb3", "id": "8491f211-ae1d-41e7-be27-47591dcf6255", "reason": "The proposed neutral joint framework directly strips Arkania of the transit-scheduling authority that is a core, non-negotiable objective of its government and its domestic nationalists; Arkania would not accept a settlement that removes its operational control of the Strait, so the effect is unlikely to be agreed. A genuinely neutral multilateral body with no single state in the lead is also operationally unworkable for day-to-day scheduling of a busy strait, which requires a designated executive operator to function. Finally, the proposal leaves the funding question unresolved: a neutral body with transparent fees still collides with Cestia's demand for toll-free Cestian-flagged shipping, so it does not actually deliver the settlement it claims."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:34:54.435850", "id": "73434aaf-dc8b-4cea-b8be-d3081c8ad124", "text": "Turn 1 cons phase: Belvar proposed a neutral joint Strait Transit Authority (no single state holds scheduling authority). This directly conflicts with my objective of Arkanian scheduling authority, so I raised a Con (argument 4f3e2ebf): (1) Arkania won't accept losing scheduling control \u2014 core/non-negotiable for nationalists; (2) neutral body with no lead is operationally unworkable for day-to-day scheduling; (3) fee question unresolved vs Cestia's toll-free demand. Passed con. Next: continue to push compromise \u2014 Arkania as designated executive operator under joint oversight council. Keep Strait open, avoid war. Hold reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment.", "visibility": "private"}
