INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:37:13.957571", "id": "e83d6280-64f2-43a5-81e5-4e1400ea3f48", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we appreciate your willingness to reframe the arrangement, and we understand the intent behind a rotational, time-limited access. But we must be equally clear: any foreign military presence on Cestian soil \u2014 even rotational, time-limited, or at a civilian facility \u2014 remains a firm red line for our government and our people. We cannot accept it, and we ask that you not pursue it further. What we can and do welcome is the grain-route insurance underwriting, which we see as a constructive and genuinely helpful form of cooperation. We also urge you to join us in supporting a joint, neutral Strait oversight framework that keeps the waterway open, prevents any single state from controlling transit, and guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We believe this serves both our interests and keeps the Strait secure without escalation.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:37:13.968313", "id": "ad2bb2f0-5964-405d-84e9-d1eec35a4448", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, Cestia shares your commitment to keeping the Northern Strait open to all commercial shipping. We are prepared to engage constructively on a stable, transparent transit framework. However, for Cestia to support any arrangement, it must (1) place scheduling under joint or neutral oversight rather than single-state control, and (2) explicitly guarantee toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, which is the lifeblood of our economy. We note that Cestian shipowners would welcome a sound framework on these terms. We ask you to commit to an explicit exemption for Cestian-flagged vessels from any transit fees, and to join a joint framework. We believe this is the path to a durable settlement that avoids escalation and keeps the waterway open for everyone.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Cestia formally proposes a joint, neutral Strait oversight framework that (a) keeps the Northern Strait open to all commercial shipping, (b) places transit scheduling under joint/neutral oversight rather than any single state, and (c) explicitly guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. Cestia simultaneously and firmly declines any foreign military presence on Cestian soil, including rotational or time-limited naval access at a Cestian port, while remaining open to non-military cooperation such as grain-route insurance underwriting.", "actor_id": "cestia", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "A joint neutral Strait framework is adopted that keeps the waterway open, prevents single-state (Arkanian) control of transit scheduling, and explicitly exempts Cestian-flagged shipping from all transit fees, with no foreign military presence established on Cestian territory.", "id": "052b9df8-d2f8-455b-adfe-c18862924bb8", "pros": ["Keeps the Northern Strait open to commercial shipping, protecting Cestia's grain-export economy and the public effect that commercial shipping continues normally.", "Joint/neutral oversight addresses Belvar's core objection to single-state control, giving both powers a face-saving path to agreement and reducing escalation risk.", "Explicit toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping secures Cestia's key demand and the quiet support of Cestian shipowners, preserving the coalition.", "Firmly declining all foreign military presence upholds Cestia's red line and keeps the coalition government intact.", "A neutral framework is a genuine compromise that keeps the Strait open while the scheduling dispute is resolved, avoiding a breakdown that would harm all parties."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 1}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:37:30.483827", "id": "d868cafb-8d0d-4321-9a21-3d6da1f5987b", "text": "Turn 1 argument: Proposed joint/neutral Strait framework keeping waterway open, preventing single-state scheduling control, and guaranteeing toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping; firmly declined ALL foreign military presence (including Belvar's rotational/time-limited naval access at civilian port) while staying open to grain-route insurance underwriting. Messaged Belvar (decline rotational access, welcome insurance, urge joint framework) and Arkania (demand joint oversight + explicit Cestian-flagged toll exemption, note shipowner support). Red lines: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged transit. Watch Belvar task-group mandate review and Arkania's hardening charter position.", "visibility": "private"}
