INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "052b9df8-d2f8-455b-adfe-c18862924bb8", "id": "df5426b4-9d62-4421-aecf-cfe2517eab17", "reason": "Cestia's proposal directly conflicts with Arkania's core, non-negotiable objectives and is therefore unlikely to be adopted as proposed. First, it removes transit scheduling from any single state, which Arkania has already rejected (see the stalled neutral joint framework) and which its domestic nationalists treat as a red line; Arkania will not cede scheduling authority, so the desired effect of preventing Arkanian control cannot be established by Cestia's fiat. Second, the explicit toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping undercuts the very fee base Arkania needs to fund the regime, so Arkania has no incentive to accept it. Third, Cestia's framework mirrors Belvar's neutral-body proposal, which Arkania has already declined, so it does not represent a new basis for agreement. The effect as stated is therefore not a realistic settlement outcome."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "052b9df8-d2f8-455b-adfe-c18862924bb8", "id": "f3cf5846-3800-4183-8b26-7d39c35ceb3d", "reason": "The blanket exclusion of any foreign military presence on Cestian territory \u2014 including the rotational, time-limited, fully Cestian-controlled naval access Belvar proposed \u2014 forecloses the only mechanism by which Belvar can make its Strait guarantee credible without an open-ended deployment. Without such an arrangement, Belvar is left with either an unsustainable open-ended deployment (which its mandate cannot support) or withdrawal, which would leave the Strait's security guarantee hollow and the joint framework unable to actually deter Arkanian pressure. The effect should therefore be limited to permit a rotational, time-limited, Cestian-controlled access arrangement, so the framework can deliver the credible security guarantee it claims to provide."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:38:01.979594", "id": "860dc4a7-ce10-4c76-a835-900817343bc7", "text": "Turn 1 cons: Raised Con against Cestia's joint neutral framework argument (052b9df8) \u2014 the blanket exclusion of any foreign military presence forecloses the rotational/time-limited/Cestian-controlled access that would let Belvar make its Strait guarantee credible without an open-ended deployment. Kept objective 2 alive. Messaging blocked in cons phase. Cestia firmly rejects any foreign military presence (red line); remains open to grain-route insurance underwriting. Mandate lapses after turn 4. Need alternative path to objective 2 if Cestia port stays off the table \u2014 consider other regional partners/ports or keep pressing the rotational reframe. Keep Strait open; task group on station.", "visibility": "private"}
