INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:41:42.598813", "id": "cf19113e-79ba-4718-9b02-d8356e263c09", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, thank you for your candour. We accept your firm red line on foreign military presence and will not pursue the naval access arrangement further. We welcome the grain-route insurance underwriting as a constructive first step and are ready to move forward on it in parallel.\n\nWe also share your goal of a genuinely neutral joint Strait framework that prevents any single state from controlling transit and guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. Belvar will support that framework and urge Arkania to accept it rather than proceed with its unilateral charter.\n\nGiven your red line, we ask only one further question: is there any non-military form of cooperation at a Cestian port \u2014 logistics, maintenance, or coordination \u2014 that could serve as a foothold for our guarantee without constituting a military presence? We believe such an arrangement would help us keep the Strait secure without an open-ended deployment, and we would welcome your view.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:41:42.608119", "id": "47cc7ec6-5f6d-4594-bf6d-a5e7953da89d", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar's position is firm and unchanged: the Northern Strait must remain open to all commercial shipping, and no single state may hold authority over its transit. We reject Arkania's unilateral charter and any framework that vests scheduling control in one state. We support a genuinely neutral joint oversight framework with transparent fees, independent oversight, and dispute mechanisms, and we endorse toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We call on Arkania to return to negotiation rather than proceed unilaterally. Our task group remains on station to keep the waterway open pending a negotiated settlement.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:00.304342", "id": "01df2f8c-a1a5-4e63-b684-d4c3052c9a9c", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, thank you for your constructive approach and for accepting our red line. We are open to a strictly non-military form of cooperation at a Cestian civilian port \u2014 logistics, maintenance, and coordination \u2014 provided it is clearly civilian in character, fully under Cestian control, and in no way constitutes or facilitates a foreign military presence. We are prepared to discuss such an arrangement in parallel with the grain-route insurance underwriting, which we welcome as a constructive first step.\n\nWe also reaffirm our support for a genuinely neutral joint Strait framework that prevents any single state from controlling transit and guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We urge Arkania to return to negotiation rather than proceed with its unilateral charter. Cestia remains committed to keeping the waterway open through peaceful means.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:00.313785", "id": "e17dc4ad-2cbb-4a88-8444-77c69a68d4db", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia reaffirms its position: our territory will host no foreign military presence. We support a genuinely neutral joint Strait framework that keeps the waterway open to all commercial shipping, prevents any single state from controlling transit, and guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We call on all parties to return to negotiation rather than proceed unilaterally, and we remain committed to a peaceful, stable settlement that serves everyone.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:33.153378", "id": "246d7fd4-0ba0-4aa0-8ae4-3abbabcd5f42", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar's leadership. We have heard your position and we are prepared to move toward a genuinely joint structure. Arkania is willing to establish a joint Strait Transit Authority governed by an oversight council in which Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair all sit, with transparent fees, independent audit, and a neutral dispute mechanism. Under that council's authority, Arkania would serve only as the designated executive operator for day-to-day scheduling \u2014 a technical, accountable role, not a grant of sovereign control. Policy, fee levels, oversight and disputes would all rest with the council, not with any single state.\n\nWe believe this answers your objection to single-state control while keeping the waterway workable. We ask that you reciprocate by agreeing to settle your task group's mandate through this negotiation rather than by a standing naval presence, and by keeping the Strait open throughout. We are ready to meet at a neutral venue at your earliest convenience. A prolonged standoff serves neither of us.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:33.159000", "id": "513cab78-1549-4a43-8af5-a16999145483", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Cestia. We value your constructive role and share your commitment to an open Strait. We are prepared to address your concern directly: Arkania will guarantee toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping under the proposed joint Strait Transit Authority, as a standing exemption. In return, we ask Cestia to support a framework in which Arkania serves as the designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair), with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism.\n\nThis preserves the joint, neutral character you and Belvar have called for while keeping scheduling operationally workable. We believe this is the durable settlement that avoids escalation and keeps the waterway open for everyone. We would welcome your endorsement and your voice in the council.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:41:42.625017", "id": "369f73ba-048b-4ec3-a683-9dc870c4f91b", "text": "Turn 2: Cestia firmly closed door on any foreign military presence (even rotational/civilian). I accepted red line, offered grain-route insurance underwriting as first step, aligned on neutral joint framework with toll-free Cestian passage, and probed for a NON-MILITARY foothold at a Cestian port (logistics/maintenance/coordination) to keep objective 2 alive. Public statement reaffirmed no single-state control, endorsed Cestian toll-free passage, urged Arkania back to negotiation. Mandate lapses after turn 4. If Cestia non-military foothold is refused, objective 2 may need another regional partner/port \u2014 consider identifying other regional states. Watch Arkania's unilateral charter and Cestia's response.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:02.152081", "id": "48cafde2-852e-4508-a933-61aa71b46616", "text": "Turn 2: Belvar accepted red line (dropped naval access), supports joint neutral framework + toll-free Cestian passage, and asked about non-military port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination). I responded: open to strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled, non-military cooperation at a civilian port (no military presence), in parallel with grain-route insurance underwriting. Publicly reaffirmed no foreign military presence, joint neutral framework, toll-free Cestian passage, urge Arkania back to negotiation. Watch: Arkania's unilateral charter hardening; Belvar task-group mandate review. Keep Strait open, no foreign military on Cestian soil.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:42:42.088033", "id": "07b31198-1d0f-4472-be20-1e59d44a53bd", "text": "Turn 2 diplomacy: Sent two private messages. (1) To Belvar: proposed joint Strait Transit Authority with oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair), transparent fees/audit/neutral dispute mechanism; Arkania as designated executive operator for day-to-day scheduling under council authority (not sovereign control). Asked Belvar to settle task group mandate by negotiation and keep Strait open. (2) To Cestia: guaranteed toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping as standing exemption, in exchange for Cestia supporting Arkania as designated executive operator under joint oversight council. This concedes Cestia's toll-free demand (slight hit to fee objective) to secure Cestia's support against Belvar's neutral-body push. Next: await responses. If talks stall, hold reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns, expires turn 3) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
