INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Arkania formally advances the joint Strait Transit Authority framework: a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, and a neutral chair) sets policy, fee levels, oversight and disputes, while Arkania serves as the designated executive operator for day-to-day transit scheduling under that council's authority. Arkania keeps the Strait open to all commercial shipping, guarantees toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged vessels as a standing exemption, and agrees to settle Belvar's task-group mandate through this negotiation rather than by force.", "actor_id": "arkania", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "A joint Strait Transit Authority is established in which a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holds policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with Arkania as the designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under that council. The Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, Cestian-flagged vessels are exempt from transit fees, and Belvar's naval task-group mandate is settled by negotiation rather than by a standing armed presence, avoiding direct armed conflict.", "id": "8cd72cac-074d-4d2c-8987-a870f2b81f8c", "pros": ["Preserves Arkanian authority over transit scheduling in practice (as executive operator) while giving Belvar a genuinely joint, non-single-state structure, directly answering its stated objection and keeping talks alive.", "Keeps the Strait open to commercial shipping, protecting the shipping revenue and economy Arkania depends on, and avoids the ruin of direct war with Belvar.", "Secures Cestia's support by guaranteeing toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, converting a blocker into an ally on the council.", "Belvar's domestic support for a prolonged deployment is assessed as weak, so a negotiated settlement of its task-group mandate is the credible path it can accept without escalation.", "The joint council with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism provides a durable, face-saving framework that all three parties can endorse."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 2}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:43:06.158605", "id": "357e5ade-2f03-4ab5-9ad9-d1d183513416", "text": "Turn 2 (post-messages): Arkania offered a genuinely joint Strait Transit Authority \u2014 oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair), transparent fees, independent audit, neutral dispute mechanism; Arkania only as \"designated executive operator\" for day-to-day scheduling under council authority. This is a real step toward joint structure, BUT it still vests Arkania with day-to-day scheduling authority \u2014 the exact crux of my objective 1 (no Arkanian authority over transit). I must not accept as-is; I need the scheduling role to be neutral/rotating or under council control, not Arkanian-executed. No messages left this phase (0 remaining) \u2014 respond next turn. Cestia open to non-military civilian port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination) + grain insurance underwriting; that may salvage objective 2 as a non-military foothold. Mandate lapses after turn 4. Keep Strait open; task group on station.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:43:18.295021", "id": "9e7eb0ae-42b5-42f7-b592-b4bb7b5ada42", "text": "Turn 2 (late): Arkania made a NEW offer (msg 513cab78): it will guarantee toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping under a joint Strait Transit Authority (standing exemption), IN RETURN for Cestia supporting Arkania as \"designated executive operator\" of day-to-day scheduling under a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania + neutral chair), with transparent fees, independent audit, neutral dispute mechanism.\n\nAssessment: This is a major concession on my toll-free demand (objective 2). BUT it asks me to endorse Arkania as executive operator of scheduling - which conflicts with my stated position and Belvar's that NO single state may control transit. Endorsing Arkania's executive-operator role could alienate Belvar and undercut the joint/neutral framework I've championed. However, Arkania frames it as under a joint oversight council, so it's not pure single-state control.\n\nStrategy: I could NOT message this phase (0 messages remaining). Next phase, respond to Arkania: welcome the toll-free exemption as constructive, but insist the executive operator role must be genuinely neutral/joint (e.g., a neutral chair or rotating/co-equal operator), not Arkania alone, to preserve the joint character and keep Belvar on board. Do not fully endorse Arkania as sole executive operator. Keep both powers engaged; avoid becoming their battlefield. Red lines unchanged: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged transit. Watch Belvar task-group mandate review and Arkania's unilateral charter hardening.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:43:34.702001", "id": "2bbe9860-945a-4ade-a3a8-62cdb521718d", "text": "Turn 2 argument submitted (8cd72cac): joint Strait Transit Authority with oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority; Arkania as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under council. Strait kept open; Cestian-flagged toll-free exemption; Belvar task-group mandate settled by negotiation. This preserves Arkanian scheduling authority in practice while giving Belvar a joint structure. Already sent private messages to Belvar and Cestia this turn. Next: await responses. If talks stall, hold reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns, plan expires turn 3) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
