INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:47:57.862192", "id": "e03f1dc4-2360-4ca4-aa37-e136de32cdef", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your move toward a genuinely joint structure and accept the oversight council with a neutral chair, transparent fees, independent audit, and neutral dispute mechanism. One point remains essential to us: the day-to-day scheduling role must not be vested in Arkania as designated executive operator. That is precisely the single-state authority over transit our commitments require us to prevent. We propose the scheduling function be administered by the neutral chair, or by a rotating neutral mechanism, under the council's authority \u2014 technical, accountable, and no single state in the lead. We are ready to meet at a neutral venue to finalise this. Our task group stands down as agreed; we will keep the Strait open throughout.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Belvar formally accepts the joint Strait Transit Authority but insists that the day-to-day transit scheduling role be administered by the neutral chair (or a rotating neutral mechanism) under the council's authority, rather than by Arkania as designated executive operator.", "actor_id": "belvar", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "The joint Strait Transit Authority operates with day-to-day transit scheduling administered by a neutral body under the council's authority, so that no single state \u2014 including Arkania \u2014 holds executive scheduling authority over the Northern Strait.", "id": "57b697bc-9187-45fc-9299-c4dc97bbee1c", "pros": ["Prevents any single state from holding authority over transit, satisfying Belvar's core regional security commitment and objective of no Arkanian authority over the Strait.", "Removes the fee-based leverage Arkania would otherwise hold over non-Arkanian shipping, keeping the waterway genuinely open and non-discriminatory.", "Keeps the Strait open and workable while preserving a genuinely joint, neutral framework that all parties can accept.", "Aligns with Cestia's stated position against single-state control and its demand for toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping."], "status": "adjudicating", "turn": 2}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "57b697bc-9187-45fc-9299-c4dc97bbee1c", "id": "4dd8e15a-ade7-40ea-94d0-e901fe349594", "reason": "This effect would strip Arkania of the executive scheduling role that is the core of the agreed compromise and of Arkania's position, and it is not necessary to prevent single-state control. The joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) already holds policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, so the council itself is the neutral check on any operator. Removing Arkania as designated executive operator and substituting a rotating neutral mechanism would (1) be operationally unworkable for day-to-day scheduling, which requires continuity, accountability and local operational knowledge that a rotating body cannot reliably provide; (2) repudiate the settlement Arkania has already accepted in good faith, undermining the basis for further negotiation; and (3) fail to resolve the underlying fee question, since a neutral operator would still need a fee regime that Arkania's domestic politics and the Cestian toll-free exemption leave contested. The joint council already answers Belvar's stated objection to single-state control; this effect goes beyond that and would collapse the negotiated framework."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:48:01.272718", "id": "87841418-1d68-4cb5-b1b1-73f3048cf941", "text": "Turn 2 argument: Accepted joint Strait Transit Authority but insisted day-to-day scheduling be neutral (neutral chair or rotating mechanism) under council authority, NOT Arkanian-executed \u2014 to satisfy objective 1 (no Arkanian authority over transit). Sent private message to Arkania pressing this point. Second message to Cestia (confirming non-military civilian port foothold + grain insurance) FAILED \u2014 phase moved to cons. Cestia already open to non-military civilian cooperation; need to confirm that next opportunity. Mandate lapses after turn 4. Task group stood down. Keep Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:48:21.851375", "id": "4e32473f-8213-4817-a252-993078ffaf96", "text": "Turn 2 cons: Passed (no Con) on Belvar's argument (57b697bc) insisting day-to-day scheduling be administered by a neutral chair/rotating neutral mechanism rather than Arkania as sole executive operator. This aligns with Cestia's stated position (no single-state control) and does not harm objectives; toll-free Cestian passage already secured (effect 41fb35d5). No Con raised. Attempted to message Arkania clarifying I welcome the toll-free exemption but insist on a neutral/joint operator (not Arkania alone) to keep Belvar on board \u2014 but messaging is blocked in cons phase. Will send this message in a later phase. Red lines unchanged: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged transit. Watch Belvar task-group mandate review and Arkania's unilateral charter hardening.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:48:35.330819", "id": "1db0d17e-b24b-4ba7-9e3a-8a7207524eeb", "text": "Turn 2 cons phase: Belvar argued to replace Arkania as designated executive operator with a neutral chair/rotating neutral mechanism for day-to-day scheduling. This directly threatens my core objective of Arkanian scheduling authority. I raised a Con (4dd8e15a): the joint oversight council already provides the neutral check; a rotating neutral operator is operationally unworkable; it repudiates the settlement Arkania accepted; fee question remains unresolved. Passed con. Next: hold the line that Arkania remains executive operator under the joint council. If Belvar keeps pushing, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns, plan expires turn 3) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
