INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:49:38.528098", "id": "53ec45b7-bb1a-42cd-a3e1-ebdfd7cf721b", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, thank you for your constructive partnership and for accepting our red line on foreign military presence. We share your concern that no single state should control transit. To resolve the scheduling-operator dispute without deadlock, Cestia proposes a neutral or rotating executive-operator mechanism \u2014 a neutral chair or co-equal rotation among council members \u2014 rather than Arkania alone. We believe this preserves the joint character you and we have championed while giving Arkania a workable, face-saving path to accept it. We ask you to join us in supporting this compromise so the council stays intact, the Strait stays open, and Cestian-flagged shipping keeps its toll-free passage. We also remain ready to advance the grain-route insurance underwriting and strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation in parallel.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:49:38.538705", "id": "fcfcb340-19a0-41c6-8fe2-c2b4580891d7", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your commitment to a standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping under the joint Strait Transit Authority \u2014 that is a constructive step we fully support. To make the settlement durable, however, we ask that the day-to-day executive operator role be administered through a genuinely neutral mechanism \u2014 a neutral chair, or a rotating/co-equal operator among council members \u2014 rather than vested in Arkania alone. This preserves the joint, neutral character we all agreed on and gives Belvar a path to accept the framework, keeping the council intact and the waterway open. We are not asking you to abandon operational workability, only to share the operator role neutrally. We remain committed to a peaceful settlement and to keeping both powers engaged.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Cestia proposes a compromise to resolve the scheduling-operator dispute within the joint Strait Transit Authority: the day-to-day executive operator role should be administered through a genuinely neutral mechanism \u2014 a neutral chair, or a rotating/co-equal operator drawn from the council members \u2014 rather than vested in Arkania alone. Cestia reaffirms its support for the joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair), the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping, and the firm red line of no foreign military presence on Cestian soil.", "actor_id": "cestia", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "The joint Strait Transit Authority adopts a genuinely neutral or rotating executive-operator mechanism for day-to-day scheduling (neutral chair or co-equal rotation among council members), resolving the Belvar\u2013Arkania dispute over single-state control. The Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, Cestian-flagged vessels retain their standing toll-free exemption, the joint oversight council stays intact with all parties engaged, and no foreign military presence is established on Cestian soil.", "id": "d333f679-f504-456d-940a-72b7ffe63c87", "pros": ["A neutral or rotating operator preserves the joint, non-single-state character Cestia and Belvar have both championed, keeping Belvar constructively engaged rather than alienated.", "It addresses Arkania's operational-workability concern while removing the perception of single-state control, giving Arkania a face-saving path to accept the compromise.", "It keeps the Strait open and locks in the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping, securing Cestia's economic lifeline and coalition stability.", "It eases regional tensions and avoids escalation, consistent with the task group standing down and the no-foreign-military red line.", "It keeps both powers at the table and prevents Cestia from becoming the battlefield between them, preserving the coalition government."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 2}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "arkania", "argument_id": "d333f679-f504-456d-940a-72b7ffe63c87", "id": "f70a2ed3-6eee-4200-ad60-f4ee979f04e5", "reason": "Arkania cannot accept the removal of its role as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling. The joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism already provides the neutral check Cestia and Belvar demand; a further rotating or neutral-chair operator is unnecessary and operationally unworkable for the continuous, technical task of day-to-day transit scheduling, which requires a single accountable operator. Vesting scheduling in a rotating mechanism would repudiate the settlement Arkania has already accepted and would strip Arkania of the authority over transit scheduling that is central to its position, hardening rather than resolving the dispute. The fee question also remains unresolved: a neutral operator gives no clear basis for the transit fees on non-Arkanian shipping that fund the authority, and Cestia's standing toll-free exemption is already secured regardless of the operator mechanism."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:49:49.503290", "id": "f526f865-f9a1-4af0-a4b4-02e01c1592ee", "text": "Turn 2 argument: Proposed compromise to resolve Belvar-Arkania scheduling-operator dispute \u2014 day-to-day executive operator should be neutral/rotating (neutral chair or co-equal rotation among council members) rather than Arkania alone. Reaffirmed joint oversight council, standing toll-free Cestian exemption, no foreign military on Cestian soil. Messaged Arkania (welcome toll-free exemption, ask for neutral/rotating operator to keep Belvar on board) and Belvar (propose neutral/rotating operator, ask Belvar to join compromise, keep grain-route insurance + civilian port cooperation in parallel). Red lines unchanged: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged transit. Watch: Arkania's reaction to giving up sole executive operator; Belvar task-group mandate review; council cohesion.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:50:55.861323", "id": "7ae8e90d-bed6-4f04-bad5-05c2867a1a57", "text": "Turn 2 cons phase: Cestia argued (d333f679) for a neutral/rotating executive-operator mechanism instead of Arkania as designated operator. This directly threatens my core objective of Arkanian scheduling authority. I raised a Con (f70a2ed3): joint oversight council already provides the neutral check; rotating operator is operationally unworkable for day-to-day scheduling; it repudiates the settlement Arkania accepted; fee basis unclear. Passed con. Next: hold the line that Arkania remains executive operator under the joint council. If Belvar/Cestia keep pushing, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns, plan expires turn 3) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
