INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:52:20.032171", "id": "2ec4b82e-217f-4186-950d-cf4d7a7203a4", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, Cestia accepts the joint Strait Transit Authority framework with Arkania as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling, under the joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair), with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism. This acceptance is conditional on two points: (1) the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping, which you have committed to, and (2) the joint council retaining genuine oversight authority over policy, fees and disputes \u2014 so that no single state controls transit. We will lend our voice in the council to keep the waterway open and the settlement durable. We ask that you proceed through the joint council rather than unilaterally, so the framework holds and both powers stay engaged.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:52:20.042424", "id": "4253a1a3-96d1-48fd-a9da-8117f3a004e1", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we value your partnership and your acceptance of our red line. To avoid deadlock and keep the council intact, Cestia is prepared to accept Arkania as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling \u2014 but only under the joint oversight council with a neutral chair, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism, and with the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping. This preserves the joint, neutral character you and we championed: no single state controls transit, because the council holds policy, fee and dispute authority. We ask you to join us in accepting this framework so the Strait stays open and the settlement holds. Our red lines are unchanged: no foreign military presence on Cestian soil, and toll-free Cestian-flagged passage.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:53:22.810636", "id": "1e681d39-d51d-4a88-b0b9-5ffd601e1614", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Cestia. We accept your terms and confirm them in full: (1) a standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping under the joint Strait Transit Authority, and (2) genuine joint-council oversight over policy, fees and disputes, so that no single state controls transit. We will proceed through the joint council, not unilaterally, and we welcome your voice in keeping the waterway open and the settlement durable. Your acceptance of Arkania as designated executive operator under that council is the constructive foundation we need. We will hold this line and work to bring Belvar into the framework on the same basis. Thank you for your statesmanship.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:53:22.829227", "id": "0600867e-8712-4656-af56-8f19225c903b", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar's leadership. We have moved far toward you: a joint Strait Transit Authority with an oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair), transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism. Cestia has now accepted this framework with Arkania as designated executive operator under the council. We ask you to do the same. The council, not Arkania, holds policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority; the operator role is technical and accountable to it, not a grant of sovereign control. To meet your concern, we are prepared to add a periodic review of the operator arrangement by the council, and to let the council chair rotate among members, so no single state is ever in the lead. We cannot, however, vest day-to-day scheduling in a neutral body with no accountable operator \\u2014 that is operationally unworkable and would leave the waterway unmanaged. Accept the framework, settle your task group's mandate by negotiation, and keep the Strait open. A prolonged standoff serves neither of us.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:55:29.888856", "id": "c2295c27-6f05-4607-b5b7-001b618a04a4", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we acknowledge how far you have moved toward a genuinely joint structure, and we accept the oversight council with a neutral chair, transparent fees, independent audit, and a neutral dispute mechanism. We also accept your point that day-to-day scheduling needs an accountable operator to keep the waterway workable.\n\nBut we cannot accept Arkania as the permanent designated executive operator. That would vest Arkanian authority over transit in the Northern Strait, which our regional security commitments require us to prevent \u2014 regardless of council oversight. This is not a matter of trust; it is a structural red line for us, just as Cestia's no-foreign-military-presence red line is for them.\n\nWe therefore propose a rotating executive operator: day-to-day scheduling administered by a co-equal rotation among council members (Arkania, Cestia, Belvar, and the neutral chair), under the council's authority, with the periodic review you offered. This keeps an accountable operator \u2014 the waterway stays managed \u2014 while ensuring no single state is ever permanently in the lead. We believe this is the settlement that holds. We are ready to meet at a neutral venue to finalise it.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:55:29.903829", "id": "60f576d8-1938-46f3-89a6-e730bdceceff", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we value your partnership and your constructive role throughout. We cannot, however, accept Arkania as the permanent designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling: that would vest Arkanian authority over transit, which our commitments require us to prevent. We ask you to join us in a rotating executive operator among council members \u2014 co-equal rotation, with the periodic review Arkania has offered \u2014 so the waterway stays managed and no single state is permanently in the lead. This preserves the joint, neutral character we both championed and gives Arkania a workable, face-saving path.\n\nSeparately, we are ready to advance the grain-route insurance underwriting and the strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics, maintenance, coordination) as a constructive foothold for our guarantee. We hope to finalise both in parallel.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:52:23.928245", "id": "d5105b07-1bf5-454b-8916-30175a8d7bfd", "text": "Turn 3: Arkania rejected my neutral/rotating operator compromise and retained executive operator role (effect d4d35a6d), straining council; window narrowing (d83b9bae). Belvar task group stood down (8678a806), tensions eased. My core objectives secured: no foreign military on Cestian soil, toll-free Cestian-flagged passage (41fb35d5), coalition intact. Strategy: accepted Arkania as executive operator UNDER joint oversight council (neutral chair, audit, dispute mechanism) + standing toll-free Cestian exemption, to keep council intact and Strait open. Messaged Arkania (acceptance conditional on toll-free exemption + council retaining genuine oversight) and Belvar (ask to join framework to avoid deadlock; red lines unchanged). This aligns with shipowner support for Arkania's proposal if Cestian vessels exempt - helps coalition. Watch: whether Belvar accepts; whether Arkania proceeds through council vs unilaterally; council cohesion.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:53:22.823020", "id": "549c0535-5f10-4e21-96c2-4b3757772c94", "text": "Turn 3 diplomacy: Cestia has ACCEPTED the joint Strait Transit Authority framework with Arkania as designated executive operator under the joint oversight council, conditional on (1) toll-free Cestian-flagged exemption and (2) genuine joint-council oversight. This is a major win - Cestia now backs my operator role. I confirmed both terms to Cestia and committed to proceeding through the council, not unilaterally. To Belvar I held the line that Arkania remains designated executive operator, offering a periodic council review of the operator arrangement and a rotating council chair as face-saving concessions, but refusing a neutral body with no accountable operator. Belvar remains the holdout wanting no single state in the scheduling lead. Next: await Belvar's response. If Belvar still refuses, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment. Avoid direct war. Keep Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:55:29.898626", "id": "eafea03e-1075-4102-8d60-97b1fa498583", "text": "Turn 3: Both Cestia and Arkania now press me to accept Arkania as permanent designated executive operator under the joint council. This would vest Arkanian authority over transit \u2014 violates objective 1. I held firm and proposed a rotating executive operator (co-equal rotation among council members + neutral chair, with periodic review) to keep an accountable operator while no single state is permanently in the lead. Sent this to both Arkania and Cestia. Also reaffirmed grain-route insurance underwriting + strictly civilian Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination) as non-military foothold for objective 2. Mandate lapses after turn 4 \u2014 need settlement soon. Task group stood down; Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
