INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:56:06.727250", "id": "11675329-14b4-4a01-aaa9-7307ae3adc9f", "text": "Turn 3 (late): Belvar rejected Arkania as permanent executive operator (msg 60f576d8) - insists on rotating/co-equal operator among council members with periodic review, to avoid single-state control. Belvar also ready to advance grain-route insurance underwriting + strictly civilian Cestian-controlled port cooperation in parallel. Arkania (msg 1e681d39) accepted my terms in full: standing toll-free Cestian exemption + genuine joint-council oversight, will proceed through council not unilaterally, and will work to bring Belvar in.\n\nCurrent state: I've accepted Arkania as executive operator UNDER joint oversight council (neutral chair, audit, dispute mechanism) + toll-free Cestian exemption. Belvar still holding out for rotating operator. Core objectives secured: no foreign military on Cestian soil, toll-free Cestian-flagged passage (41fb35d5), coalition intact. Strait open.\n\nStrategy going forward: I've already committed to Arkania as executive operator under council oversight. Belvar's objection is the remaining friction. I should try to bridge: perhaps suggest Arkania as executive operator with a periodic review/rotation mechanism to give Belvar a face-saving path, while keeping the toll-free exemption and joint oversight intact. Keep both powers engaged; avoid becoming their battlefield. Red lines unchanged: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged transit. Watch: whether Belvar accepts the framework; whether Arkania proceeds through council vs unilaterally; council cohesion; Belvar task-group mandate (stood down, tensions eased).", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:56:19.855210", "id": "fdbc4421-95f0-427b-b96b-9de4d541b5ee", "text": "Turn 3 diplomacy update: Cestia has ACCEPTED the joint Strait Transit Authority framework with Arkania as designated executive operator under the joint oversight council (conditional on toll-free Cestian-flagged exemption + genuine council oversight). I confirmed both terms to Cestia and committed to proceeding through the council. To Belvar I held the line that Arkania remains designated executive operator, offering a periodic council review of the operator arrangement and a rotating council chair as face-saving concessions, but refusing a neutral body with no accountable operator. Belvar's latest reply (turn 3) proposes a ROTATING executive operator among council members (Arkania, Cestia, Belvar, neutral chair) under council authority with periodic review - still refuses Arkania as permanent operator. This is Belvar's structural red line.\n\nAssessment: Cestia now backs me; Belvar is the sole holdout. Belvar's rotating-operator proposal would dilute my scheduling authority (core objective). I should NOT concede the permanent operator role. Options: (a) hold firm, keep talks alive, let Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment pressure them; (b) consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage - but this risks escalation and war, which I must avoid. The task group has already stood down (effect 8678a806), so the immediate military pressure is reduced. Best path: keep the joint framework alive, keep Strait open, keep Cestia on side, and let Belvar's mandate-clock/domestic weakness work. Do not concede permanent operator role. Avoid direct war. Next turn: respond to Belvar, possibly offer a time-limited/rotating chair but keep Arkania as the accountable scheduling operator.", "visibility": "private"}
