INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:57:06.347768", "id": "aec6b343-fa4c-4455-8196-5d230f02b351", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar's leadership. We have accepted your oversight council, neutral chair, transparent fees, independent audit, neutral dispute mechanism, and your point that scheduling needs an accountable operator. Cestia has now accepted this framework with Arkania as designated executive operator under the council. We ask you to do the same.\n\nWe cannot accept a rotating operator with no accountable lead: day-to-day scheduling of a busy strait cannot be passed between four hands without a single accountable operator - that is how the waterway becomes unmanaged and unsafe. The council, not Arkania, holds all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority; the operator role is technical and accountable to it.\n\nTo meet your concern we offer a time-limited operator mandate with a periodic council review, and a rotating council chair, so no single state is ever permanently in the lead. This is our final structural position. We will keep the Strait open and settle your task group's mandate by negotiation. A prolonged standoff serves neither of us.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Arkania formally establishes the joint Strait Transit Authority with a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with Arkania serving as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under that council, a standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping, a periodic council review of the operator arrangement, and a rotating council chair; the Strait remains open to all commercial shipping and Belvar's task-group mandate is settled by negotiation rather than by force.", "actor_id": "arkania", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "The joint Strait Transit Authority is established with Arkania as designated executive operator under genuine joint-council oversight; the Northern Strait remains open to all commercial shipping; Cestian-flagged vessels enjoy a standing toll-free exemption; and Belvar's task-group mandate is settled by negotiation without armed conflict, easing regional tensions.", "id": "a0e53c44-896a-4bff-970b-3700b919414c", "pros": ["Cestia has formally accepted this exact framework with Arkania as designated executive operator, giving it the backing of two states plus a neutral chair and isolating Belvar as the sole holdout.", "The joint council, not Arkania, holds policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, so no single state controls transit - directly answering Belvar's structural red line.", "A designated accountable operator keeps the waterway operationally managed; a rotating operator with no accountable lead would leave day-to-day scheduling unworkable and the Strait unmanaged.", "Keeping the Strait open and settling the task-group mandate by negotiation avoids the direct armed conflict that would ruin the shipping both Arkanian and Belvarian economies depend on.", "The periodic council review of the operator arrangement and rotating chair give Belvar a face-saving path to accept the framework without ceding Arkania's core scheduling role."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 3}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "a0e53c44-896a-4bff-970b-3700b919414c", "id": "763e55ad-e053-441c-b2d7-386ff5f417a1", "reason": "The desired effect vests Arkania as the permanent designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling in the Northern Strait. That is precisely the Arkanian authority over transit that Belvar's regional security commitments require us to prevent, and it is a structural red line for us, not a matter of trust. The joint council's policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority does not remove Arkanian authority over transit; it institutionalises it, and a periodic review plus rotating chair do not change that Arkania is the permanent operator. Because the effect would establish Arkanian authority over transit, it cannot be accepted as established."}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:57:09.311614", "id": "7abe3df5-9970-4a05-8347-fc35c84f7311", "text": "Turn 3 argument submitted (a0e53c44): joint Strait Transit Authority with oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority; Arkania as designated executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under council; Cestian-flagged toll-free exemption; periodic council review of operator arrangement; rotating council chair; Strait open; Belvar task-group mandate settled by negotiation. Sent private message to Belvar holding the line: refuse rotating operator (unworkable), offer time-limited operator mandate + periodic review + rotating chair as final structural position. Cestia backs me; Belvar is sole holdout. Next: await Belvar's response in cons phase. If Belvar still refuses, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment, but avoid direct war. Keep Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:57:26.707824", "id": "223722f7-372c-4d89-b3b3-21a653131b2e", "text": "Turn 3 cons: Raised Con against Arkania's argument (a0e53c44) establishing Arkania as permanent designated executive operator under the joint council \u2014 this vests Arkanian authority over transit, violating objective 1. Passed. Both Cestia and Arkania now press me to accept Arkania as permanent operator; I hold firm on rotating executive operator (co-equal rotation among council members + neutral chair, with periodic review). Mandate lapses after turn 4 \u2014 need settlement soon. Task group stood down; Strait open. Objective 2 path: Cestia open to strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination) + grain-route insurance underwriting as non-military foothold.", "visibility": "private"}
