INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T13:59:00.936658", "id": "fc6f356c-b49f-43bd-a239-dc0da0f347ea", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we accept the joint Strait framework as settled and will honour the council's authority, the open Strait, and toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We ask now to finalise the two constructive tracks you have welcomed: (1) the grain-route insurance underwriting, and (2) a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation arrangement (logistics, maintenance, coordination) at a Cestian civilian port, fully under your control and in no way constituting or facilitating a foreign military presence. This gives Belvar a standing, peaceful foothold to make its Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet or open-ended deployment, while respecting your red line. We are ready to conclude both in parallel.", "turn": 3, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Belvar concludes with Cestia a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation agreement (logistics, maintenance, coordination) at a Cestian civilian port, and underwrites the grain route's insurance, as a non-military foothold for its Strait guarantee.", "actor_id": "belvar", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "Belvar secures a standing non-military foothold at a Cestian port that makes its Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet or an open-ended deployment, while fully respecting Cestia's red line on foreign military presence.", "id": "93093e12-f352-4f4c-8589-afe8a337fbe4", "pros": ["Cestia has already signalled openness to strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics, maintenance, coordination) and to grain-route insurance underwriting, so this is a mutually acceptable next step.", "It fully respects Cestia's firm red line on no foreign military presence, preserving the partnership and the negotiated settlement.", "It gives Belvar a standing foothold to sustain a credible Strait guarantee without a permanent fleet or open-ended deployment, satisfying its security commitments and avoiding a renewed standoff.", "It strengthens the joint framework by giving Belvar a concrete, peaceful stake in keeping the Strait open and stable, complementing the council's authority.", "It advances the settlement and reduces the risk of escalation, supporting the open Strait and toll-free Cestian-flagged passage."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 3}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T13:59:05.365857", "id": "a151f0ce-f8ab-44b1-9dd3-3fc0425439c7", "text": "Turn 3 (argument): Joint Strait framework settled with Arkania as designated executive operator under a joint oversight council (policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority with council; periodic review; rotating chair). I accept this as satisfying objective 1 (no Arkanian authority over transit \u2014 council holds real authority). Task group stood down; Strait open; Cestian toll-free passage. My argument this turn: conclude strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination) + grain-route insurance underwriting as a non-military foothold for objective 2 (standing naval access blocked by Cestia's red line; pivoting to non-military foothold) and objective 3 (avoid open-ended deployment). Sent private message to Cestia confirming both tracks. Public message failed (phase moved to cons). Mandate lapses after turn 4 \u2014 need the Cestian foothold finalised soon.", "visibility": "private"}
