INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Cestia reaffirms its full commitment to the joint Strait Transit Authority and, to keep both powers engaged and ease regional tensions, offers Belvar a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation arrangement (logistics, maintenance, coordination) at a Cestian civilian port \u2014 fully under Cestian control, time-limited and renewable only by Cestia, and in no way constituting or facilitating a foreign military presence.", "actor_id": "cestia", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "The joint Strait framework remains durable: the joint oversight council retains genuine policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority; the Strait stays open to all commercial shipping; Cestian-flagged vessels keep their standing toll-free exemption; no foreign military presence appears on Cestian soil; and regional tensions ease as Belvar gains a peaceful, non-military stake in the settlement while Arkania's executive-operator role proceeds under council oversight.", "id": "2d24c10b-a855-49ac-b236-4bc0a83aff36", "pros": ["Gives Belvar a peaceful, non-military foothold to make its Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet or open-ended deployment, easing tensions and keeping both powers engaged rather than making Cestia their battlefield.", "The arrangement is strictly civilian and fully under Cestian control, with clear notice and duration limits and no foreign garrison or base, fully respecting the red line of no foreign military presence on Cestian soil and preserving the coalition.", "Keeps the joint council intact and the settlement durable, preventing any single state from controlling transit while giving Arkania a workable executive-operator role under genuine council oversight.", "Secures the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged shipping and the open Strait, protecting the grain economy that holds the coalition together.", "Reduces the risk of escalation by giving both powers a constructive stake in a negotiated, peaceful settlement, consistent with Cestia's commitment to keep the waterway open through negotiation."], "status": "adjudicating", "turn": 3}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:03:47.861459", "id": "6c36f491-69ca-47c9-92fa-983d8827a905", "text": "Turn 3 argument (2d24c10b): Reaffirmed commitment to joint Strait Transit Authority and offered Belvar a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation arrangement (logistics/maintenance/coordination) at a Cestian civilian port \u2014 fully under Cestian control, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, non-military \u2014 to give Belvar a peaceful stake, ease tensions, and keep both powers engaged. Also ready to advance grain-route insurance underwriting in parallel. Red lines unchanged: no foreign military on Cestian soil; toll-free Cestian-flagged passage. Messaging blocked in this phase (running/cons) \u2014 could not send bridge messages to Belvar/Arkania; will send next phase. Core objectives secured: no foreign military (effect 4fb9ae4e), toll-free Cestian passage (01ef9fc9), coalition intact. Watch: whether Belvar accepts the civilian cooperation and the joint framework; whether Arkania proceeds through council vs unilaterally; council cohesion; tensions remain elevated (53155b03).", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:04:13.782857", "id": "d667e90b-35dd-4016-a562-eaed2fb5a17f", "text": "Turn 3 cons phase: Cestia's argument (2d24c10b) reaffirms the joint Strait Transit Authority with Arkania as designated executive operator under the joint oversight council, and offers Belvar a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation arrangement (logistics/maintenance/coordination, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, no foreign military presence). This effect SERVES Arkania: it keeps the joint framework with my operator role intact, keeps Cestia on side, and gives Belvar a peaceful non-military stake that reduces their pressure for a rotating operator. No Con raised; passed. Next: hold the line that Arkania remains the accountable scheduling operator under the council. If Belvar still refuses, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage given Belvar's weak domestic support for prolonged deployment, but avoid direct war. Keep Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:04:39.202036", "id": "e09efea1-6ec3-4276-8aff-f1150739f49a", "text": "Turn 3 cons: Passed on Cestia's argument (2d24c10b) \u2014 it offers a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination) at a Cestian civilian port, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, no foreign military presence. This serves objective 2 (non-military foothold since naval access is blocked by Cestia's red line) and objective 3 (avoid open-ended deployment), while keeping Strait open, council authority intact, Cestian toll-free passage, and no Arkanian authority over transit. No Con raised. Messaging blocked in cons phase. Mandate lapses after turn 4 \u2014 need the Cestian civilian foothold + grain insurance underwriting finalised next turn. Task group stood down; Strait open.", "visibility": "private"}
