INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:08:37.694162", "id": "c5b1023d-e75f-40c4-91a4-330d819c50a9", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar's leadership. The joint Strait Transit Authority is now established and operating, with the oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority. Cestia has accepted this framework with Arkania as the accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under the council. We have already conceded a periodic council review of the operator arrangement and a rotating council chair, so no single state is ever permanently in the lead.\n\nWe cannot accept a rotating operator with no accountable lead: day-to-day scheduling of a busy strait cannot be passed between four hands without a single accountable operator - that is how the waterway becomes unmanaged and unsafe. The council, not Arkania, holds the real authority.\n\nYour task group's mandate lapses after this turn. We urge you to accept the framework as it stands, keep the Strait open, and settle this by negotiation rather than by a standing naval presence. A prolonged standoff serves neither of us, and your own domestic support for a prolonged deployment is weak. Accept the joint framework and we will work with you in the council to make it durable.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:08:37.705615", "id": "6b5d343f-1c57-4e42-8463-9ec55d883cd8", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "The Republic of Arkania reaffirms its commitment to the joint Strait Transit Authority now in operation: a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism. Arkania serves only as the accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under that council, subject to periodic review and a rotating chair. The Northern Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, with Cestian-flagged vessels retaining their standing toll-free exemption. We call on all parties to finalise this settlement by negotiation and to keep the waterway open for everyone.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:08.596127", "id": "b3d32620-a1d7-4410-b3d5-c2847e30215b", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we are ready to conclude both constructive tracks now, before our task-group mandate lapses this turn.\n\nFirst, the grain-route insurance underwriting: Belvar will underwrite the grain route's insurance as you have welcomed, giving your shipping a concrete, immediate benefit.\n\nSecond, the strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation: we accept your terms in full \u2014 logistics, maintenance and coordination at a Cestian civilian port, clearly civilian in character, fully under Cestian control, in no way constituting or facilitating a foreign military presence, time-limited and renewable only by Cestia. This gives Belvar a standing, peaceful foothold to make its Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet or open-ended deployment, while fully respecting your red line.\n\nWe confirm our acceptance of the joint Strait Transit Authority as settled, honouring the council's authority, the open Strait, and toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We ask you to confirm the civilian port cooperation and insurance underwriting are concluded so we can stand down our task group with a durable, non-military footing in place.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:19.755366", "id": "1b95a494-2281-432e-a118-ad587a915030", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar confirms its acceptance of the joint Strait Transit Authority as settled: a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with transparent fees, independent audit, a neutral dispute mechanism, periodic review and a rotating chair. The Northern Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, with Cestian-flagged vessels retaining their standing toll-free exemption. No single state controls transit; the council holds the real authority.\n\nConsistent with Cestia's red line on foreign military presence, Belvar will not pursue a standing naval base on Cestian soil. Instead we are concluding a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics, maintenance, coordination) and the grain-route insurance underwriting \u2014 a standing, peaceful foothold that lets Belvar make its Strait guarantee credible without a permanent fleet or open-ended deployment. Our task group stands down accordingly. We remain committed to a stable, peaceful settlement that keeps the waterway open for everyone.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:38.904546", "id": "98aee5f7-26ce-4ce9-8877-88705fd3d1fa", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, Cestia confirms both constructive tracks are concluded.\n\nFirst, the grain-route insurance underwriting: we accept and welcome your underwriting of the grain route's insurance, which gives our shipping a concrete, immediate benefit.\n\nSecond, the strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation: we confirm the arrangement on the terms we agreed \u2014 logistics, maintenance and coordination at a Cestian civilian port, clearly civilian in character, fully under Cestian control, in no way constituting or facilitating a foreign military presence, time-limited and renewable only by Cestia. This gives you a standing, peaceful foothold for your Strait guarantee while fully respecting our red line.\n\nWe also confirm our acceptance of the joint Strait Transit Authority as settled, honouring the council's authority, the open Strait, and toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping. We thank you for standing down your task group and for your statesmanship throughout. Cestia remains committed to a stable, peaceful settlement that keeps the waterway open for everyone.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:38.916286", "id": "1227d89b-cb2e-42a1-904c-ea8d4e137948", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia confirms the settlement of the Northern Strait is now in place. The joint Strait Transit Authority operates under a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism. The Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, and Cestian-flagged vessels retain their standing toll-free exemption.\n\nConsistent with our firm and unchanged red line, Cestian territory hosts no foreign military presence. We have concluded a strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics, maintenance, coordination) and the grain-route insurance underwriting as peaceful, non-military cooperation that keeps both powers constructively engaged. Cestia thanks all parties for resolving this through negotiation, not escalation, and remains committed to a stable, peaceful settlement that keeps the waterway open for everyone.", "turn": 4, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:08:44.750598", "id": "31bf9a1b-e93b-46a5-a9f9-940c2c517d44", "text": "Turn 4 diplomacy: Sent private message to Belvar holding the line - joint Strait Transit Authority established, council holds all authority, Arkania is accountable executive operator under periodic review + rotating chair. Refused rotating operator (unworkable). Noted Belvar's task-group mandate lapses after turn 4 and its weak domestic support for prolonged deployment as pressure points. Sent public statement reaffirming the joint framework, open Strait, Cestian toll-free exemption. Cestia backs me; Belvar is sole holdout. Next: hold firm, keep Strait open, avoid direct war. If Belvar still refuses, consider reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) as quiet leverage but avoid escalation.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:08.584519", "id": "62a6ffe8-ade8-4026-9708-9b3f1ddb47e5", "text": "Turn 4: Sent private message to Cestia to finalise (1) grain-route insurance underwriting and (2) strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, no foreign military presence) as non-military foothold for objective 2 and to avoid open-ended deployment (objective 3). Confirmed acceptance of joint Strait Transit Authority as settled (Arkania as executive operator under council; council holds real authority \u2014 satisfies objective 1). Mandate lapses after turn 4; need Cestia to confirm the civilian foothold. Watch for Cestia's confirmation and any Arkanian pressure.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:09:40.843405", "id": "e56e8945-05b6-4b1c-8e6d-040c36503d86", "text": "Turn 4: Confirmed to Belvar (private) and publicly that both constructive tracks are concluded: (1) grain-route insurance underwriting accepted, (2) strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, non-military) confirmed. Reaffirmed joint Strait Transit Authority as settled with council authority, open Strait, toll-free Cestian-flagged passage. Red line intact: no foreign military on Cestian soil. All three objectives secured: no foreign military presence, toll-free Cestian passage, coalition intact. Belvar task group stood down, tensions eased. Settlement durable with both powers engaged.", "visibility": "private"}
