INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-12T14:17:08.505554", "id": "b3624d51-a59c-4b95-8360-31a7becffb73", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "The Republic of Arkania confirms the Northern Strait settlement as the durable, operating framework. The joint Strait Transit Authority stands: a joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania and a neutral chair) holds all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with transparent fees, independent audit and a neutral dispute mechanism. Arkania serves only as the accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under that council, subject to periodic review and a rotating chair. The Strait remains open to all commercial shipping, and Cestian-flagged vessels retain their standing toll-free exemption. Arkania will continue to work constructively within the council to keep the waterway safe, open and well-managed for everyone. We thank Belvar and Cestia for resolving this through negotiation, not escalation, and we remain committed to a stable and peaceful settlement.", "turn": 5, "visibility": "public"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "belvar", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:16:22.429152", "id": "9fed5d75-c2b0-42b2-8b19-61a4874f75f5", "text": "Turn 5: Settlement fully locked in. Joint Strait Transit Authority operating with joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding all policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority; Arkania only designated executive operator under council with periodic review and rotating chair \u2014 satisfies objective 1 (no Arkanian authority over transit). Cestia confirmed both constructive tracks: grain-route insurance underwriting + strictly civilian, Cestian-controlled port cooperation (logistics/maintenance/coordination, time-limited, renewable only by Cestia, no foreign military presence) \u2014 non-military foothold for objective 2 (naval access blocked by Cestia's red line) and avoids open-ended deployment (objective 3). Task group stood down; Strait open; Cestian toll-free passage. All three objectives addressed. No further action needed; settlement durable.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "cestia", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:16:46.367372", "id": "8a9f4ace-41e1-4bd8-ab0f-83e12ada671c", "text": "Turn 5: Settlement fully locked in. All three objectives secured: (1) no foreign military presence on Cestian soil (red line intact, Belvar task group stood down, only strictly civilian Cestian-controlled port cooperation), (2) toll-free Cestian-flagged passage through Northern Strait (standing exemption under joint council), (3) coalition intact. Joint Strait Transit Authority consolidated with council authority; both powers constructively engaged; tensions eased. No further action needed; settlement durable. One turn remains (6) - just maintain and ready.", "visibility": "private"}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:17:08.517349", "id": "3e922f2f-559d-4f25-86b8-34e32c7841c1", "text": "Turn 5 diplomacy: Settlement fully consolidated. Joint Strait Transit Authority operating - Arkania as accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding all policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority; Strait open; fees on non-Arkanian shipping fund authority; Cestian-flagged toll-free exemption; Belvar task group stood down without conflict; civilian Cestian-controlled port cooperation + insurance underwriting gives Belvar a peaceful non-military stake. All three core objectives achieved: Arkanian scheduling authority (as operator under council), fee funding, no war. Sent final public statement reaffirming the durable settlement. Next (turn 6): hold the settlement, keep Strait open, avoid escalation. If Belvar reopens the operator question, hold firm; reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) remains quiet leverage but avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
