INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=argument data={"action": "Arkania formally ratifies and commits to the consolidated Northern Strait settlement as the durable, final operating framework: the joint Strait Transit Authority under the joint oversight council (Belvar, Cestia, Arkania, neutral chair) holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, with Arkania as the accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling subject to periodic council review and a rotating chair; the Strait kept open to all commercial shipping; transit fees on non-Arkanian shipping funding the authority; and the standing toll-free exemption for Cestian-flagged vessels.", "actor_id": "arkania", "budget_slot": 1, "desired_effect": "The Northern Strait settlement is locked in as the settled, durable operating regime: the joint Strait Transit Authority continues to operate with the joint oversight council holding all policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, Arkania serving as the accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under periodic review and a rotating chair, the Strait remaining open to all commercial shipping, transit fees on non-Arkanian shipping funding the authority, and Cestian-flagged vessels retaining their standing toll-free exemption; all parties remain constructively engaged and the waterway stays open and well-managed without armed conflict.", "id": "01bf4fbf-68b7-40f5-bb8d-c9de24667ee3", "pros": ["The settlement already stands as the operating regime (effects 9ad5cf52, 3d13c830) and all parties have publicly accepted it; this argument consolidates rather than reopens it, preserving stability.", "It secures Arkania's core objective of scheduling authority in practice (as accountable executive operator under the council) while the council holds the real policy, fee, oversight and dispute authority, so no single state controls transit.", "It preserves the fee funding on non-Arkanian shipping that finances the authority, and the Cestian toll-free exemption that keeps Cestia on side.", "It keeps the Strait open to all commercial shipping and avoids any armed conflict with Belvar, whose task group has already stood down, consistent with Arkania's objective of avoiding direct war.", "It gives Belvar a peaceful, non-military stake (civilian port cooperation and insurance underwriting) and Cestia its red line, so all three powers remain constructively engaged in a durable framework."], "status": "open_for_cons", "turn": 5}
INFO     agents.autonomous:autonomous.py:281 autonomous record kind=note data={"actor_id": "arkania", "created_at": "2026-09-12T14:17:22.726435", "id": "324bf39c-69c3-45c8-a10f-a326e720fcb4", "text": "Turn 5 argument submitted (01bf4fbf): formally ratified and committed to the consolidated Northern Strait settlement as the durable final framework - joint oversight council holds all policy/fee/oversight/dispute authority, Arkania as accountable executive operator of day-to-day scheduling under periodic review + rotating chair, Strait open, fees on non-Arkanian shipping fund authority, Cestian toll-free exemption. All three core objectives achieved: Arkanian scheduling authority (as operator under council), fee funding, no war. Settlement fully consolidated with all parties constructively engaged. Next (turn 6): hold the settlement, keep Strait open, avoid escalation. If Belvar reopens the operator question, hold firm; reserve mobilisation (needs 2 turns) remains quiet leverage but avoid direct war.", "visibility": "private"}
